## 8. Read uncertainty output

<p class="ryg-part"><span class="ryg-label ryg-yellow">YELLOW</span> AI may assist with `summary()`/`confint()` syntax or output organization; verify all numerical values against R.</p>
<p class="ryg-part"><span class="ryg-label ryg-red">RED</span> Interpret the standard error, interval, p-value, and null hypothesis in context independently.</p>

Use `summary(bike_model)` and `confint(bike_model)`. Report for `temperature_c`:

- the estimate;
- standard error;
- 95% confidence interval;
- p-value and the null hypothesis tested by that p-value.

Interpret the standard error, confidence interval, and p-value in context.

```{r}
