summary(bike_model)
confint(bike_model)
```

**In the temperature_c row, we see the estimate is 161.968, the standard error is 7.444, and the p value is <2e-16, while the 95% CI is (147.35,176.58). The standard error being much smaller compared to the estimate means the regression line can be considered to be a pretty good estimate slope, and the p value being super small means we can reject the idea that the slope is zero, we know it is positive. The 95% CI in context means that for an increase in 1 degree temperature, we estimate there is a 95% confidence that the number of rentals would increase by between 147.35 and 176.58 daily on average.**

